@{
    ViewBag.Title = "PetCare";
} 

<style>

    .card {
        height: 100%;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 12px;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
        background-color: #fff;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        max-height: 400px;
        overflow: hidden;
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, max-height 0.2s ease-in-out;
    }

        .card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-8px);
            box-shadow: 0 20px 45px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
            z-index: 10;
            max-height: 700px;
            overflow: visible;
        }

        .card img {
            width: 100%;
            height: 200px;
            object-fit: cover;
            border-top-left-radius: 12px;
            border-top-right-radius: 12px;
        }

    .card-body {
        padding: 25px 22px;
        flex-grow: 1;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: space-between;
    }

    .card-title {
        font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #333;
        margin-top: 0;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
        line-height: 1.4;
        display: -webkit-box;
        -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
        -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
        overflow: hidden;
        transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }

    .card:hover .card-title {
        -webkit-line-clamp: unset;
        overflow: visible;
        margin-bottom: 15px;
    }

    .card-text {
        transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }

        .card-text .blog-paragraph {
            font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: #777;
            line-height: 1.5;
            margin-bottom: 0;
            display: -webkit-box;
            -webkit-line-clamp: 3;
            -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
            overflow: hidden;
            transition: all 0.4s ease-out;
        }

    .card:hover .card-text .blog-paragraph {
        -webkit-line-clamp: unset;
        overflow: visible;
    }

    .entry-item.col-md-4 {
        padding-left: 10px;
        padding-right: 10px;
        margin-bottom: 30px;
    }
</style>

<div class="container">
    <div class="row pt-5 pb-3">
        <div class="entry-item col-md-4">
            <div class="card position-relative">
                <img src="~/images/Care/care8.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="Pet Cancer Support Image">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title">When Your Pet Is Facing Cancer: Support and Resources</h3>
                    <div class="card-text">
                        <p class="blog-paragraph">
                            we know how worrying that can be.
                            Many cancers can still be managed with proper care,
                            so watching for changes in behavior, lumps, or appetite remains important.
                            For treatment options and support, you can visit <span class="fw-bold"> PETLY Veterinary Hospital on Abu Nusayr St. 222 Amman </span>,
                            their team is ready to help you and your pet through this. Early detection is key to successful treatment.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="entry-item col-md-4">
            <div class="card position-relative">
                <img src="~/images/Care/care6.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="Another Pet-Related Topic Image">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title">If Your Pet is Facing Kidney Issues: Diet, Hydration & Support</h3>
                    <div class="card-text">
                        <p class="blog-paragraph">
                            Chronic kidney disease (CKD) can be worrying,
                            but with early detection and management, your pet can still have a good quality of life.
                            The focus is on monitoring blood work, managing diet (low protein/phosphorus),
                            and ensuring proper hydration. For specialized diagnosis and treatment plans,
                            including advanced laboratory testing and dietary counseling, you can visit the
                            <span class="fw-bold">Humane Center for Animal Welfare Veterinary Clinic in Amman</span>.
                            Their dedicated team offers comprehensive care to slow the disease's progression.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="entry-item col-md-4">
            <div class="card position-relative">
                <img src="~/images/Care/care3.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="Pet Health & Wellness Image">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title">The Absolute Importance of Routine Vaccinations</h3>
                    <div class="card-text">
                        <p class="blog-paragraph">
                            Protect your furry friend from common and serious diseases like Parvovirus and Rabies.
                            Routine vaccination schedules are personalized for your pet's lifestyle and age.
                            Schedule an appointment with
                            <span class="fw-bold">First Pet Veterinary Clinic on Abed Al-Raheem Al-Hhaj Mohammad St.11 Amman </span>
                            for a comprehensive health check-up and vaccine review.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="entry-item col-md-4">
            <div class="card position-relative">
                <img src="~/images/Care/care9.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="Pet Health & Wellness Image">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title">Managing Pet Diabetes: Symptoms, Insulin, and Monitoring</h3>
                    <div class="card-text">
                        <p class="blog-paragraph">
                            Diabetes is a manageable condition,
                            but it requires commitment. Watch for increased thirst and urination, weight loss, and changes in appetite. Successful management depends on a strict regimen of daily insulin injections,
                            a consistent diet, and careful blood glucose monitoring. For diagnosis,
                            setting up an initial treatment plan, and long-term metabolic control, you can visit
                            <span class="fw-bold">Vetzone Pet Health Center, located in Mecca St. 5, Amman</span>.
                            They offer expert guidance to stabilize your pet’s sugar levels and improve their overall health.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="entry-item col-md-4">
            <div class="card position-relative">
                <img src="~/images/Care/care7.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="Pet Health & Wellness Image">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title">Rabbit Health Crisis: Recognizing and Treating GI Stasis</h3>
                    <div class="card-text">
                        <p class="blog-paragraph">
                            GI Stasis is a life-threatening emergency often caused by pain, stress,
                            or a low-fiber diet. Symptoms include a sudden refusal to eat,
                            absence of fecal pellets, and a hunched posture (indicating pain).
                            This condition is often complicated by dehydration and liver issues.
                            If your rabbit stops eating for more than 4–6 hours,
                            seek immediate veterinary attention. For expert diagnosis
                            and emergency critical care, you can visit
                            <span class="fw-bold">Best Friend Veterinary Clinic on 7th circle, Zahran St, Amman</span>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="entry-item col-md-4">
            <div class="card position-relative">
                <img src="~/images/Care/care4.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="Pet Health & Wellness Image">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title">Canine Ehrlichiosis: Recognizing and Treating</h3>
                    <div class="card-text">
                        <p class="blog-paragraph">
                            Ehrlichiosis is a bacterial infection transmitted by ticks.
                            Symptoms can vary widely but often include fever, lethargy, poor appetite, and sometimes nosebleeds.
                            It can progress to a chronic phase, affecting bone marrow and requiring long-term treatment.
                            Regular tick prevention is essential. Diagnosis requires a blood test, and treatment involves a
                            specific course of antibiotics. For diagnosis and management of this prevalent condition, consult with
                            <span class="fw-bold">TURQUOISE vet clinic Wasfi At Tall St.</span>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="entry-item col-md-4">
            <div class="card position-relative">
                <img src="~/images/Care/care2.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="Pet Health & Wellness Image">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title">Feline Hyperthyroidism: Symptoms and Treatment Options</h3>
                    <div class="card-text">
                        <p class="blog-paragraph">
                            Hyperthyroidism is caused by the overproduction of thyroid hormones,
                            common in cats over 10 years old. signs are dramatic weight loss despite having a huge appetite,
                            increased thirst, and restlessness. Diagnosis is confirmed with a simple blood test.
                            For long-term management, including medication, special diets,
                            , you can consult with
                            <span class="fw-bold">Best Friend Veterinary Clinic on 7th circle, Zahran St, Amman</span>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="entry-item col-md-4">
            <div class="card position-relative">
                <img src="~/images/Care/care5.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="Pet Health & Wellness Image">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title">Pacheco’s Disease in birds Causes, Signs, and Risks </h3>
                    <div class="card-text">
                        <p class="blog-paragraph">
                            It's' a severe, rapidly progressing herpesvirus that causes high
                            mortality in parrots. Often, the first sign is sudden death, but milder symptoms
                            can include lethargy, feather plucking, and bright yellow-green diarrhea.
                            It is highly contagious among flocks. Immediate diagnosis through lab testing is crucial for
                            quarantine and potential antiviral treatment. For expert avian diagnostics and intensive care
                            , you can contact the <span class="fw-bold">International Veterinary Center in Amman</span>,
                            a facility often equipped for exotic pet emergencies.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="entry-item col-md-4">
            <div class="card position-relative">
                <img src="~/images/Care/care10.jpg" class="img-fluid" alt="Pet Health & Wellness Image">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title">FIP in Cats: Recognizing Symptoms and Hope for Treatment</h3>
                    <div class="card-text">
                        <p class="blog-paragraph">
                            FIP, caused by a mutation of Feline Coronavirus,
                            was once universally fatal,
                            but it can often be treated.
                            Symptoms vary widely and can include persistent fever,
                            weight loss, and fluid buildup in the abdomen ("wet FIP").
                            Diagnosis requires advanced testing to confirm
                            the mutated virus. If you suspect FIP
                            , seek a clinic with access to the latest
                            research and diagnostic tools.
                            For specialized feline and internal medicine support,
                            you can visit the
                            <span class="fw-bold">Best Friend Veterinary Clinic on 7th circle, Zahran St, Amman</span>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<script src="js/jquery-1.11.0.min.js"></script>
